    "body": "Stopped after the same real gate failure occurred twice, as instructed.\n\nThe ASCII DXF reader and its tests are implemented locally.\nThe work is UNCOMMITTED in /home/mikekinney/CamcraftPool/.claude/worktrees/issue-1860 on issue/1860-dxf-reader.\nThe branch itself still points to the starting base, 62e1d36a.\nNo changes were pushed and no PR was opened.\n\nAll 46 DXF tests passed.\nThe initial tests failed to compile because upstream had no dxf module.\nRestoring the upstream lib.rs reproduced that failure in both suites, and restoring the reader made them pass.\n78 runtime mutation experiments failed as intended and passed after restoration.\nTwo individual checks were redundant: missing INSUNITS is also checked at the end of HEADER, and callers only finish vertices that have X.\nRemoving both missing-INSUNITS checks was covered by a failing runtime mutation.\nExplicit geometry clippy passed after an equivalent float-literal spelling fix in a test.\n\nThe required quick gate expanded to batch.\nThe app test a_tapered_punch_is_refused_at_post_while_the_file_states_no_guide_heights failed in sodick_alc400g.\nThe UI trace_composite test binary also exited with SIGSEGV.\nThe exact Sodick test failed again when run alone through the gate.\nNo unrelated fix, merge, rebase, or refresh was attempted.\n\nDuring the long gate, the shared upstream/main reference advanced to 8719d8b7.\nIt now contains 0e1f3709, which fixes the Sodick test for #1856.\nThis worktree remains on 62e1d36a.\nThis does not mean #1860 is already fixed.\n\nEvidence is in /tmp/1860-red-before.txt, /tmp/1860-mutation-inventory.json, /tmp/1860-mutations/, /tmp/1860-gate-quick.txt, /tmp/1860-geometry-clippy.txt, and /tmp/1860-sodick-rerun.txt.\nDetailed gate logs remain in the worktree under gate-logs/quick-20261115-131600/ and gate-logs/test-20261115-141313/.\nThe claim is released.\nWork stopped before the decision ledger, self-review, and push steps.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
